  "chapter": {
    "number": 36,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(37) A Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Fret not yourself because of evil-doers, neither be envious of them that do iniquity.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For they shall soon be withered as the grass, and shall soon fall away as the green herbs.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Hope in the Lord, and do good; and dwell on the land, and you shall be fed with the wealth of it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Delight yourself in the Lord; and he shall grant you the requests of your heart.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Disclose your way to the Lord, and hope in him; and he shall bring it to pass.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he shall bring forth your righteousness as the light, and your judgment as the noon-day.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Submit yourself to the Lord, and supplicate him: fret not yourself because of him that prospers in his way, at the man that does unlawful deeds.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "ease from anger, and forsake wrath: fret not yourself so as to do evil.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For evil-doers shall be destroyed: but they that wait on the Lord, they shall inherit the land.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And yet a little while, and the sinner shall not be, and you shall seek for his place, and shall not find it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But the meek shall inherit the earth; and shall delight themselves in the abundance of peace.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The sinner will watch for the righteous, and gnash his teeth upon him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But the Lord shall laugh at him: for he foresees that his day will come.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Sinners have drawn their swords, they have bent their bow, to cast down the poor and needy one, and to kill the upright in heart.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let their sword enter into their own heart, and their bows be broken.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "A little is better to the righteous than abundant wealth of sinners.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the arms of sinners shall be broken; but the Lord supports the righteous.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord knows the ways of the perfect; and their inheritance shall be for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They shall not be ashamed in an evil time; and in days of famine they shall be satisfied.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the sinners shall perish; and the enemies of the Lord at the moment of their being honored and exalted have utterly vanished like smoke.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The sinner borrows, and will not pay again: but the righteous has compassion, and gives.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For they that bless him shall inherit the earth; and they that curse him shall be utterly destroyed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The steps of a man are rightly ordered by the Lord: and he will take pleasure in his way.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 24,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "When he falls, he shall not be ruined: for the Lord supports his hand.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 25,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I was once young, indeed I am now old; yet I have not seen the righteous forsaken, nor his seed seeking bread.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 26,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He is merciful, and lends continually; and his seed shall be",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 69
          },
          {
            "text": "blessed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 27,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Turn aside from evil, and do good; and dwell for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 28,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the Lord loves judgment, and will not forsake his saints; they shall be preserved for ever: the blameless shall be",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 70
          },
          {
            "text": "avenged, but the seed of the ungodly shall be utterly destroyed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 29,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But the righteous shall inherit the earth, and dwell upon it for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 30,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The mouth of the righteous will meditate wisdom, and his tongue will speak of judgment.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 31,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The law of his God is in his heart; and his steps shall not",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 71
          },
          {
            "text": "slide.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 32,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The sinner watches the righteous, and seeks to kill him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 33,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But the Lord will not leave him in his hands, nor by any means condemn him when he is judged.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 34,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Wait on the Lord, and keep his way, and he shall exalt you to inherit the land: when the wicked are destroyed, you shall see it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 35,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I saw the ungodly very highly exalting himself, and lifting himself up like the cedars of Libanus.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 36,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Yet I passed by, and behold! he was not: and I sought him, but his place was not found.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 37,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Maintain innocence, and behold uprightness: for there is a remnant to the peaceful man.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 38,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But the transgressors shall be utterly destroyed together: the remnants of the ungodly shall be utterly destroyed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 39,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But the salvation of the righteous is of the Lord; and he is their defender in the time of affliction.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 40,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And the Lord shall help them, and deliver them: and he shall rescue them from sinners, and save them, because they have hoped in him.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 69,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. for a blessing.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 36,
          "verse": 26
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 70,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, cleared in judgement.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 36,
          "verse": 28
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 71,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. be tripped up, or supplanted.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 36,
          "verse": 31
        }
      }
    ]
  },
